WEBVTT

00:07.920 --> 00:11.010
To alleviate concerns about
the increasing terrorism, the introduction

00:08.090 --> 00:12.740
Cafeteria closed for summer vacation

00:11.090 --> 00:14.050
of a special counter-terrorist mobile unit
referred to as the White Ride Unit

00:14.130 --> 00:17.050
was approved by the Cabinet,
under the direction of the GGP.

00:17.140 --> 00:20.770
Discussions about its specific
introduction date are now underway.

00:21.890 --> 00:25.480
Given that the terrorists are using
highly-agile RideBacks against us,

00:25.560 --> 00:29.440
I believe we have no choice
but to utilize this option.

00:29.530 --> 00:34.530
Preventing these terrorist attacks
is what's most important.

00:34.610 --> 00:37.820
I'm amazed you can work in this horrible heat.

00:37.910 --> 00:40.580
I told you the club's activities are canceled.

00:40.660 --> 00:45.670
There's only one man who I'll let tell me what to do.

00:51.090 --> 00:54.670
In terms of equipment,
White Rides are more like weapons

00:54.760 --> 00:56.300
than they are police vehicles.

00:56.390 --> 01:01.060
It's possible that this could lead to
the militarization of the police force.

01:01.140 --> 01:02.470
Thank you for your time.

01:05.190 --> 01:10.690
Not even I could've pulled off
moves like that. But she was able to.

01:10.770 --> 01:14.860
I couldn't control it well,
but Rin, a complete rookie, could.

01:14.950 --> 01:16.860
Just what are Fuegos?

01:16.950 --> 01:20.200
You don't need to know. It's none of your concern.

01:20.280 --> 01:24.660
It is! We're members of the same RideBack club!

01:27.170 --> 01:30.250
I at least have the right to know.

03:09.350 --> 03:12.190
Huh? You're not coming in?

03:12.270 --> 03:15.110
Today's the deadline for that gang story, you know.

03:15.190 --> 03:18.320
Can't do it. I'm about to
do some research in Toranomon.

03:18.400 --> 03:21.860
Put on the answering machine
and close up to keep 'em off our backs.

03:21.950 --> 03:22.990
Roger.

03:23.070 --> 03:25.490
Oh, I found something you'll like.

03:25.580 --> 03:29.040
--What is it?
--The mystery RideBack girl.

03:29.750 --> 03:33.040
She's a student at the same school as Tamayo Kataoka.

03:33.130 --> 03:34.960
Her name's Rin Ogata.

03:35.040 --> 03:38.880
She's got long, black hair. It's definitely her.

03:42.010 --> 03:43.090
Black hair?

03:43.180 --> 03:46.330
I've edited it so much that it's burned into my brain.

03:46.890 --> 03:47.810
What should we do?

03:47.890 --> 03:52.020
After we finish this story,
should we contact the college and ask for--

03:52.100 --> 03:53.140
Hello?

03:55.230 --> 03:57.270
<i>No, I have to look into it.</i>

04:27.300 --> 04:30.010
Kenji didn't come...

04:38.110 --> 04:40.150
Hey, Kenji. Are you home?

04:42.280 --> 04:43.780
Stinks like a guy...

04:47.950 --> 04:50.240
What is this...?

04:55.870 --> 04:57.670
"RideBack..."

05:05.090 --> 05:07.470
I didn't know Kenji read books like this...

05:23.150 --> 05:26.240
Urgh. What could Kenji be doing?

05:26.320 --> 05:29.820
He was ten when Yuki passed away...

05:30.740 --> 05:35.750
He lost his mother too soon,
before he'd had a chance to grow up.

05:35.830 --> 05:39.210
But he could at least visit her grave...

05:39.290 --> 05:41.790
That's just how boys are.

05:43.760 --> 05:46.970
It's already been six summers since then...

05:50.180 --> 05:54.060
Rin. Have you gotten into anything new at college?

05:55.480 --> 06:02.310
No, umm, nothing special, really...
I joined an ordinary clique...

06:02.400 --> 06:09.740
I'm glad. Whatever you find
a passion in is sure to be wonderful.

06:11.660 --> 06:16.290
How's dorm life? Are you and Shoko getting along?

06:16.370 --> 06:19.620
Yes! We're going to meet up later today, actually.

06:25.130 --> 06:27.050
Oh! Sweet!

06:27.130 --> 06:28.420
All right!

06:30.260 --> 06:31.890
Where'd you get these?

06:31.970 --> 06:37.520
All I know is they were smuggled in
from overseas through the black market.

06:37.600 --> 06:39.480
You sure we can have four?

06:41.400 --> 06:45.270
All I ask is that you give 'em plenty of trouble!

06:45.360 --> 06:49.450
Destroying a couple of cop cars should be a cinch.

06:49.530 --> 06:52.740
And here's a bonus.

06:52.820 --> 06:54.080
What's that?

06:54.160 --> 06:57.750
Specially-made flares that the military and BMA use.

06:57.830 --> 06:59.870
I'll let you figure out how to use 'em.

07:00.870 --> 07:02.330
Go all out.

07:02.420 --> 07:04.840
W-Wow...

07:04.920 --> 07:08.090
This is the latest model Gremlin!

07:08.170 --> 07:10.930
These are really expensive, too...

07:11.010 --> 07:13.720
It's missing its manufacturer emblem.

07:13.800 --> 07:16.510
Was it smuggled right out of the factory?

07:16.600 --> 07:19.640
I'm not sure this is a good idea after all...

07:19.730 --> 07:22.100
--It doesn't matter to you.
--But...

07:22.190 --> 07:24.400
Just teach us how to ride.

07:25.690 --> 07:29.280
A D-Dumont-made EW band...!

07:31.200 --> 07:34.740
Yes. Yes. Four machines, as planned.

07:34.830 --> 07:37.200
I'll let 'em run loose tonight.

07:37.830 --> 07:41.870
I've identified two of the three
who escaped aboard their machines.

07:41.960 --> 07:44.250
One is Abraham Ronstadt,

07:44.330 --> 07:47.130
a former special tactics soldier in the U.S. Army.

07:48.170 --> 07:50.300
The other's name is unknown.

07:50.380 --> 07:54.640
He's a South African member
of a French mercenary group.

07:54.720 --> 07:59.310
The last one was not in
our database and could not be identified.

08:00.270 --> 08:04.060
This image is from immediately
after the man launched a rocket.

08:05.810 --> 08:07.360
Magnifying.

08:11.950 --> 08:15.950
He's a European Caucasian,
according to skeletal analysis.

08:16.030 --> 08:20.490
His ability to use a rocket
while on an unstable RideBack

08:20.580 --> 08:24.540
would also suggest that he is
a highly-trained and experienced soldier.

08:29.630 --> 08:32.050
The fact that such a highly-skilled professional

08:32.130 --> 08:34.510
was deployed near the scene of the incident

08:34.590 --> 08:38.510
is evidence that the BMA is
no longer content with being a terrorist group

08:38.600 --> 08:41.640
and now seeks serious militarization.

08:41.730 --> 08:46.520
Plotting an even larger attack than
before would not be out of the question.

08:46.610 --> 08:49.020
It is the recommendation of this military research lab

08:49.110 --> 08:52.030
that RideBacks be introduced into the police force

08:52.110 --> 08:55.030
in all major cities and ports as quickly as possible

08:55.110 --> 08:58.490
in order to nip the buds of any attack plans.

09:23.640 --> 09:27.520
Sorry I'm late. I missed the bus.

09:27.170 --> 09:33.590
Please don't drop your trash here.

09:27.170 --> 09:33.590
Take your trash home with you!

09:27.610 --> 09:29.820
No, I'm sorry for being so selfish.

09:29.900 --> 09:33.610
I just suddenly felt like coming here again.

09:33.690 --> 09:36.860
Yeah. I can understand.

09:45.040 --> 09:49.250
Do you remember when we lit fireworks here

09:49.330 --> 09:50.960
after our graduation party last year?

09:51.040 --> 09:52.000
Yeah.

09:53.260 --> 09:58.050
We made so much noise that
a policeman started yelling at us

09:58.130 --> 10:00.430
and we all ran off...

10:01.300 --> 10:06.480
Then I got separated from you. It was really scary...

10:06.560 --> 10:09.140
It was pitch dark and you could only hear the waves.

10:09.230 --> 10:13.650
I kept whispering out to you as I walked...

10:13.730 --> 10:17.400
I was so happy when I finally found you!

10:17.490 --> 10:20.530
You had stayed behind to look for me, too!

10:21.740 --> 10:29.210
We hugged and cried, but
looking back, it was a pretty nice memory!

10:30.920 --> 10:34.170
Rin. You're gifted when it comes to ballet,

10:34.250 --> 10:36.840
but you have zero talent as an actor.

10:38.550 --> 10:41.340
Don't make a fuss over me. It's really weird.

10:41.430 --> 10:45.560
I was in shock before, but I'm okay now.

10:45.640 --> 10:49.480
But you said you don't want to go to crowded places...

10:49.560 --> 10:56.780
I feel like you wouldn't have
been hurt if I hadn't done that...

10:59.820 --> 11:02.070
Thanks, Rin.

11:02.160 --> 11:03.780
Shoko...

11:03.870 --> 11:07.540
Oh, no. I need to catch my bus home. How about yours?

11:07.620 --> 11:11.290
O-Oh, twenty more minutes, I think.

11:11.370 --> 11:14.170
Sorry, then. I better go, I have to run to catch it.

11:14.250 --> 11:15.920
O-Okay...

11:19.130 --> 11:21.380
I'll call you tomorrow!

11:28.220 --> 11:29.640
Found her.

11:33.690 --> 11:35.810
Whoa, this is great!

11:35.900 --> 11:37.690
It's got a great sound!

11:39.610 --> 11:42.400
Okay! Let's haul ass!

12:01.050 --> 12:03.050
Rin Ogata, right?

12:04.340 --> 12:07.640
Remember me? I visited your club the other day.

12:07.720 --> 12:11.310
I was wondering if you had a moment to talk.

12:11.390 --> 12:14.350
I'm sorry. I'm in a hurry.

12:14.440 --> 12:15.980
Hey, wait...

12:24.740 --> 12:26.740
A biker gang...

12:26.830 --> 12:28.450
RideBacks?!

12:35.330 --> 12:36.630
Kenji?!

13:15.040 --> 13:16.460
Want a ride?

13:24.470 --> 13:27.340
Damn, that's dangerous!

13:32.560 --> 13:34.520
You damn punks!

13:35.100 --> 13:36.980
Let's go all out!

13:42.690 --> 13:45.490
Don't you think this is going too far...?!

13:45.570 --> 13:47.070
It'll be fine!

13:50.660 --> 13:53.950
No worries. Show 'em who's boss!

13:54.750 --> 13:58.920
Pull your vehicles over at once and cut your engines!

13:59.000 --> 14:00.380
Yeah, right.

14:04.800 --> 14:06.010
That showed 'em!

14:06.090 --> 14:08.380
Th-That was a cop car...!

14:29.280 --> 14:31.910
The person you have called is currently unavailable.

14:38.160 --> 14:40.920
I'm sorry. I think it was my younger brother.

14:41.000 --> 14:43.880
So brother and sister are both troublemakers.

14:45.800 --> 14:47.260
I'm just kidding.

14:51.470 --> 14:54.850
They even took on police officers...

15:00.060 --> 15:03.190
Hello, there! Did something happen?

15:03.270 --> 15:06.940
This road is closed. You'll have to go around.

15:07.030 --> 15:11.530
I'm a reporter. I happened
to see some smoke nearby, so...

15:11.610 --> 15:14.410
May I see your identification?

15:17.040 --> 15:21.210
I'm sorry, but I would need
to see official press authorization first.

15:21.290 --> 15:23.000
<i>The GGP...?</i>

15:23.080 --> 15:25.460
--Excuse me...
--Understood!

15:25.550 --> 15:27.250
Sorry to bother you!

15:35.310 --> 15:38.180
<i>Sounds like I've hit upon an unexpected scoop.</i>

15:42.100 --> 15:44.610
Hold on. It's gonna get bumpy.

15:51.740 --> 15:57.870
The gang is moving from
the Inamura area to Landfill #47.

15:57.950 --> 16:01.830
Simple destruction of property
and reckless driving won't be enough.

16:01.910 --> 16:06.880
It's no problem. We can always
trump up their charges later. Can't we?

16:06.960 --> 16:08.460
Well, I suppose...

16:09.710 --> 16:14.340
Damn. Those GGP underlings think they're so great...

16:15.300 --> 16:18.560
They've been driven into the sealed area.
Two machines now on standby.

16:19.770 --> 16:24.060
Colonel. The field deployment
shakedown test is about to begin.

16:24.150 --> 16:26.560
Would you like to watch in the strategy room?

16:26.650 --> 16:31.230
No, I believe I'll watch the action from my office.

16:35.780 --> 16:38.740
Shall I inform our superiors?

16:38.830 --> 16:41.120
No, that won't be necessary yet.

16:41.200 --> 16:45.870
He's just a terrorist. We'll simply
kill him again when we find him.

17:04.600 --> 17:06.400
They're pathetic!

17:09.320 --> 17:10.980
What are those?!

17:15.910 --> 17:17.450
What the...?

17:17.530 --> 17:19.320
Those are RideBacks!

17:26.750 --> 17:28.920
Damn it! See how you like this!

17:34.050 --> 17:35.510
Shit! They tricked us!

17:35.590 --> 17:38.470
--This is bad!
--You idiot! Go faster!

17:44.600 --> 17:46.180
K-Kizaki!

17:56.780 --> 17:57.820
Kenji!

17:59.030 --> 18:00.780
Police RideBacks...?

18:00.870 --> 18:04.080
They haven't been adopted yet... What's going on?

18:06.120 --> 18:08.080
Oww...!

18:10.290 --> 18:12.590
I-I surrender!

18:20.090 --> 18:24.060
That's going too far,
even if they were a biker gang...!

18:31.400 --> 18:33.110
Shit!

18:48.250 --> 18:50.210
How did I get into this?!

18:51.750 --> 18:53.960
Take mercy on me!

18:54.050 --> 18:55.750
I'm a goner!

19:01.260 --> 19:02.390
Hey!

19:22.070 --> 19:23.280
Kenji!

19:24.030 --> 19:25.580
Oh, no...

19:32.880 --> 19:35.590
What are you doing?! Come back!

19:45.850 --> 19:47.140
Please!

19:48.850 --> 19:50.140
It started!

20:07.080 --> 20:08.450
Rin Ogata?

20:08.540 --> 20:10.250
Why is she there?

20:13.790 --> 20:17.960
That rider is the terrorist who
broke through the GGP security net.

20:18.050 --> 20:19.630
Show no mercy.

20:21.010 --> 20:23.300
<i>This will make for a great test...</i>

20:27.310 --> 20:28.680
Sister...?

20:30.310 --> 20:31.430
Kenji!

20:42.780 --> 20:45.110
--She dodged again?!
--That's absurd!

20:45.200 --> 20:46.820
Impossible!

20:49.200 --> 20:50.910
S-Sister...

20:51.000 --> 20:52.370
Kenji...!

21:02.470 --> 21:05.630
The RideBack girl...

21:36.370 --> 21:43.630
That's far enough! Cut the engine
at once and get off the RideBack!

21:43.710 --> 21:49.090
I repeat, cut the engine
at once and get off the RideBack!

21:56.730 --> 22:01.400
Even when he laughs

22:03.400 --> 22:08.990
I'm thinking of you before I realize it

22:12.030 --> 22:17.040
And the hands holding his

22:18.830 --> 22:24.300
feel your warmth, too

22:26.470 --> 22:30.220
Even if I cut out my recollections

22:30.300 --> 22:34.180
and drive them out of my heart

22:34.270 --> 22:37.930
or try to kick the memories out

22:38.020 --> 22:42.400
I still think of you

22:42.480 --> 22:46.900
Time now passes and seasons fly by

22:46.990 --> 22:50.740
Even if that smile starts to become hazy

22:50.820 --> 22:54.740
my heart will never forget you

22:54.830 --> 22:58.500
(even if we can never meet again)

22:58.580 --> 23:02.330
Even if I knock over photos of us smiling

23:02.420 --> 23:06.760
or try to hide my overflowing feelings

23:07.720 --> 23:10.970
my heart will never forget

23:11.680 --> 23:14.930
my memories with you

23:25.960 --> 23:40.980
New Hishida Theatre

23:27.150 --> 23:30.740
They caught her! They caught her!
What's going to happen now?!

23:30.820 --> 23:31.740
Hishida!

23:31.820 --> 23:34.490
Is there anything powerless people like us can do

23:34.580 --> 23:37.200
against enormous government power?

23:35.830 --> 23:39.520
Next Episode:

23:35.830 --> 23:39.520
Crime and Punishment

23:37.290 --> 23:40.000
Hishida's gone bye-bye. The end!
